flowchart TB
  accTitle: Bounded synthesis runtime
  accDescr: Durable state remains outside individual model calls. Memory and skill stores propose candidates. A bounded workspace admits content for inference. The language model proposes and interprets. Specialized governors control intention, resources, recovery, and skill execution. External actions produce observations. Typed failures create recovery state, and attributed outcomes may update future policies.
  subgraph DURABLE[Durable state outside model calls]
    I[Intentions]
    M[Memory]
    S[Skills]
    U[Uncertainty and budgets]
    Q[Recovery state and action history]
  end
  M --> CAND[Memory and skill candidates]
  S --> CAND
  CAND --> W[Bounded workspace admission]
  W --> LLM[Model proposal and interpretation]
  LLM --> GOV[Specialized governors]
  I --> GOV
  U --> GOV
  Q --> GOV
  GOV --> EXEC[Authorized skill or tool execution]
  EXEC --> OBS[Observed and verified outcome]
  OBS --> LEARN[Attributed learning updates]
  LEARN -.-> M
  LEARN -.-> S
  LEARN -.-> W
  classDef durable fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.4px
  classDef process fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.4px
  classDef outcome fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.2px
  class I,M,S,U,Q durable
  class CAND,W,LLM,GOV,EXEC process
  class OBS,LEARN outcome
